 Ruujd by case of Bing v. Atlantic Coast Line Railroad Co., ante.\n2. Reheabing refused.\nBefore Gage, J., Barnwell, December, 1909.\nAffirmed.\nAction by D. C. Burckhalter against Atlantic Coast Line Railroad Co. From judgment for plaintiff, defendant appeals.\nMessrs. Barron, Moore & Barron, Wyman & Wymcm, and Douglass McKay, for appellant.\nMessrs. R:C. Holman and W. H. Townsend, contra.\nThe opinion in this case was filed July 18, 1910, but held up on petition for rehearing until\nAugust 8, 1910."}, "file_name": "0532-01", "first_page_order": 542, "last_page_order": 542}